WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.780
Hello and welcome to the first episode of Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.460
Horror stories cooked to perfection with a splash of red sauce.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.160
My name is CZ, and I will be your server this episode.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.260
Before I get into the menu, let me tell you a little bit about this series.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:33.380
Al Dente Creepypasta will feature quality narrations of completely original stories that you won't find anywhere else.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:42.720
Each tale will be presented with chill inducing sound design and original music compositions for a production value that will go unparalleled on YouTube.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.060
These stories are longer than what you are used to on CZsWorld.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:52.600
Feel free to listen to them at work, while getting stuff done around the house, in the car, or if you are feeling brave...

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.580
...as you fall asleep at night.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.980
Today you'll be getting a three course meal with a theme of Halloween Horror Stories.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.480
I know you're hungry, so let's dig right in.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.040
One. The forbidden house.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:15.660
This is a story that happened several years back when Trick-or-Treating with my friend Alex, my older brother, John, and his friend, Evan.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:20.940
Every neighborhood has that one house that nobody ever wants to trick-or-treat at.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:29.160
Whether it be because of bad candy, mean owners, a dentist house, fear... or otherwise...

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:36.980
In this case, our parents told us we could go off on our own this year as long as we stayed together and agreed not to go to that house.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:44.820
I was in fourth grade that year and the idea of getting to go off on our own was exciting to me at the time, so naturally, I agreed.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.580
When Alex and Evan got to our house, we waited around and answered the door for a while.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.320
Trying to scare some of the younger trick-or-treaters.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:59.040
Eventually, after our parents took our baby sister to some of the houses, we grabbed our pillowcases and set off to get some candy.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:05.720
We lived in a pretty safe neighborhood, so it was common for kids our age -- or even younger --  to go out alone.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:16.060
Looking back now, I had grown up in a borderline pretentious suburbia neighborhood, the type of community you'd see in movies like Donnie Darko or American Beauty.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:23.520
Almost everyone in our neighborhood had decorations, and those who didn't had these decorative wooden ghosts nailed to the side of their mailbox.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:30.760
They were more of a cutesy decoration than scary, but they did give a nice uniformity to all the houses in the neighborhood.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.460
It was starting to get dark when we reached the house that our parents told us not to go to.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:45.920
This wasn't your stereotypical dark manor at the end of the block, but it was a little further away from the street than many of the other houses, and sort of tucked back behind some trees.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:52.100
I suggested that we go back to our house to dump whatever candy we had off before hitting up another neighborhood,

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.520
but John and the others were curious to see what the big deal was about the dark house.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.060
I'll have to admit, I was quite curious about why our parents didn't want us going over there,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:07.960
and it did seem harmless enough, so I figured they would have no way of knowing if we quickly hit this house.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.500
The driveway was long and dark, and there was no light coming from the house whatsoever.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.200
This was one of those houses where the front door was more on the side of the house,

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.500
with a curved path leading back up to the front.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:23.680
I noticed that this house did not have the wood ghost nailed to the mailbox like every other house in the neighborhood.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.560
As we walked up, I was starting to get a little nervous and I told John that I didn't think anyone was home,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.900
but he thought I was just trying to chicken out and continued on anyways.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.840
We reached the house and John loudly banged on the door.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:40.720
It was taking forever, and I was fairly convinced that the guy wasn't home or didn't want to deal with trick-or-treaters.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:48.720
Just as I was ready to turn and give up on the house, we all fell silent as the sound of footsteps could be heard on the other side of the door.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.480
While this did make me nervous,

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.800
I was also excited to see what was on the other side of the door,

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.380
that made my parents so worried about this house.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.000
So I stepped back a little bit, giving myself some room to run if need be.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.020
The door opened... revealing...

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.800
an older man with a kane.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:18.060
This immediately alleviated some of my anxiety, as it would be pretty easy to run if need be.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:25.280
The man was actually very nice and told us that we were the first visitors of the night and that he didn't expect to see many trick-or-treaters this year.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:32.560
Apparently, he lived alone and had had some kind of dispute with the neighborhood homeowner's association over the upkeep of his property.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.360
So many of the adults were trying to get back at him by excluding him from all the neighborhood festivities.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.360
He seemed like such a nice guy, and we actually felt pretty bad for him.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.320
We all wished him a happy Halloween before going on our way.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.360
I had felt silly about being nervous about visiting this house...

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.940
at least...

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.180
...that's how I felt before what happened next...

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.980
As we walked down the path back to the street side of the house,

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:02.660
I happened to glance at the upstairs window, and saw a man in a black hood peaking out from behind the window frame.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.680
As soon as I made eye contact with him, he moved back out of sight.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.600
My stomach immediately dropped,

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.060
as the man had just said that he lived alone.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.300
I bolted as I told the guys to run,

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.880
but John and Evan seemed convinced that I was just being a baby.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.660
I tried to quickly tell them that there was man in the window, but I don't think they believed me.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:29.360
However, John, being the older of the two of us, was supposed to keep an eye on me, so when I made a mad dash back towards our house,

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.180
he effectively gave chase.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.180
I knew in the back of my mind that although the old man may not have been mobile,

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:40.120
that this other guy was most likely a fully capable adult, who probably would be able to catch us,

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.400
so I didn't stop until I was inside the door.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:47.300
My parents had just returned from taking my sister out for a round of the neighborhood,

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.780
and they could immediately see that there was something wrong.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:58.380
Not wanting to get in trouble for disobeying them, I lied and told them that we were walking by the house when I saw a man in black climbing through the window of the old man's house,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.080
and that he had seen us catching him in the act.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.820
Apparently, this was a pretty good cover story, as it was enough to get my Mom to call the cops and

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.660
and the four of us locked inside the house for the rest of the night.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.840
The other guys were pretty bummed out to have our trick-or-treating cut short,

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.860
and we decided we'd watch a movie and begin trade negotiations on our candy a little early this year.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:20.840
I had a hard time paying attention to the movie, and kept looking back to the window

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.520
thinking about what the possibility might be that the guy tracked us here.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.240
Not much later that night,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:32.180
we learned that the police had searched the old man's house, and found a 19 year old man hiding in the closet with a knife.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:39.020
Apparently, the intruder had no idea who lived there, and decided to break in after seeing that the house was completely dark and

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.900
being avoided by trick-or-treaters on Halloween night.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.400
The old man was also unharmed.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:49.820
But years later I still shutter to think about what could have gone down that night.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:55.420
What if I had seen the intruder on the way up to the house before learning that the old man lived alone?

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:59.820
What if the intruder had been on the first floor and decided to give chase to us?

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.040
But what chills me the most...

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.940
is what would have happened to that nice old man,

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.980
if we had never trick-or-treated at his house?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.160
Two. The Scarecrow.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:25.460
I'll always remember 7th grade Halloween as one of the last good, innocent years of trick-or-treating with my friends,

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:30.680
before the paradigm shift to haunted houses, parties, slutty costumes, boys and alcohol.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:37.540
I'll also remember it though, for one other reason, that I haven't been able to erase from my mind since that night

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.520
I remember that day. It was Friday, so almost everyone wore their costumes to school.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.960
Jane, Margret and I had decided to go as the Powerpuff Girls,

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:50.280
even though the show was long since irrelevant at the time.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:54.120
Jane was Bubbles, Margret went as Buttercup, and I,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.340
being the only one without the correct hair color,

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.920
wore a red wig to become Blossom.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.860
During homeroom, everyone was showing off their costumes.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:06.180
One of our guy friends, Chris, was the only one who didn't wear his costume to school.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:11.580
Chris was one of the more popular guys that we knew, so I found it kind of strange that he hadn't dressed up.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:18.560
When Margret asked him why he didn't wear a costume, he just told us that we'd have to stop by his place tonight if we wanted to see his costume.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:23.420
We got the idea that whatever he was wearing, was obviously too graphic to be brought to school,

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:26.640
and made plans to swing by and check it out some time that evening.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.220
By the time we made it to Chris's house, it was starting to get pretty late.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:34.860
I figured we had about an hour or so of trick-or-treating left before we had to call it a night.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.180
We were a bigger group of girls now, probably six or seven of us. All in costume.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.780
His house didn't seem to have much in terms of decoration,

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:49.500
Just a few of those Halloween store cobwebs you see on the porch and a scarecrow sitting on a bench near the front door.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.460
Someone rang the bell and Chris's mom showed up dressed in regular clothes with a witch hat.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.260
Which I'm pretty sure she wore on multiple years.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.460
As we picked out candy, Margret asked if Chris was home,

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:04.580
but his Mom told us he had gone out to scare some trick-or-treaters with a couple friends.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:10.160
I was the last one in line to take a piece of candy, so I thanked her and we went on our way.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:16.000
As we walked back to the sidewalk, I felt something behind me tug on my wig...

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:22.920
pulling it off my head a little bit. I looked back and screamed when I saw the scarecrow standing just a couple inches behind me.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:30.020
A couple of the girls let out screams as well when they turned around and noticed the scarecrow had moved from the bench and snuck up behind us.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:37.580
Margret seemed to be the first one to come to the realization that it was Chris, who had dressed up and waited for us inside the scarecrow.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:41.280
When Jane asked how long he had to wait there, he didn't say anything,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.540
and just stared at us which admittedly made me a little bit uncomfortable.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.140
But I tried not to show it,

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.400
not wanting to give the known prankster any satisfaction.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:55.700
I guess he didn't want to break character, because even as we invited him to come trick-or-treat

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.920
at a few more houses, he remained silent for the rest of the time.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:04.400
Jane and I poked fun at him for trying too hard to be Mr. Creepy-Mysterious,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.480
trying to get him to crack or laugh or something,

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.100
but it didn't work.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:16.000
He just followed us from house to house for another block or so until we all decided to go back to my house and hang out for a while.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:21.260
He would occasionally tug on my wig, but I tried not to react, because I knew that was exactly what he wanted.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:26.720
So we stayed up late, seeing as how tomorrow was a Saturday and we could sleep in as long as we wanted.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:35.220
One of the girls went home, but the rest of us, and Chris, stayed up to watch a scary movie, which ended up not being so scary.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:40.380
Chris didn't even seem to want to watch the movie, he just stared at us the entire time.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:45.300
I knew he was just trying to freak me out, so I ignored him and tried to pay attention to the movie.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.020
I was bored and fell asleep about 20 minutes in.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:52.060
When I woke up, it was around 3 in the morning, and everyone else passed out on the couch.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.000
Chris, however, was gone.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.760
I figured that he wouldn't be able to mess with us anymore and (he) walked home.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.600
When we got back to school on Monday we confronted Chris about his little stunt on Halloween.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:09.840
He got this confused expression on his face and told us that his family didn't own a scarecrow.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.400
Or a scarecrow costume.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.920
And that he had been out all evening trick-or-treating with his friends.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:20.560
He even showed us a picture of his group, with him wearing a Jeff the Killer costume.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:25.240
He seemed to have no idea what we were talking about when we brought up the scarecrow.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:31.800
A couple of his friends even served as his alibis, saying that they were with Chris the entire night.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:40.520
To this day, I don't know if this was an elaborate prank, or if some stranger actually followed us around all night.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:53.580
But what really bothers me most to think about, is the possibility that this guy came into my house, and after all of us were asleep, left without taking anything or saying a word.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:59.640
I've never seen that particular scarecrow costume again, and to this day...

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.660
I've never gotten Chris to admit that he was behind it.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:13.100
Number Three. Costume Shop.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:23.280
I know Halloween is supposed to be a spooky holiday, but my first Halloween experience left me with scars and nightmares for years to come.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:29.100
Having moved to the USA when I was 17, I had never actually celebrated Halloween before

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:32.300
because it wasn't even a known holiday in my home country.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:36.320
A few years later, when I got my first job as a computer consultant,

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.760
I wanted to do whatever I could to get ahead and move up in the company.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.660
When my boss mentioned that there would be a company Halloween party,

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:47.280
I saw this as an opportunity to impress by finding the best costume in the office.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:54.820
I wanted to avoid the cheap quality of pop up Halloween stores, so I found a nice costume rental shop with some supposedly higher quality wares.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.320
I headed over there after staying late at work that night.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:02.240
It was pretty far away in the middle of nowhere, but I was hoping it would be worth the extra miles.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.300
I got in there about an hour before close.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.180
But to my surprise, the place was pretty much empty.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:13.020
There was only one customer in there, despite the fact that we were already pretty late into October.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:20.300
I wasn't exactly sure what I wanted to go as, so the owner of the store helped me pick out several costumes that I was intersted in,

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.100
and let me into the changing room to see how they all looked on me.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.920
I started to get undressed when I heard the door chime,

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.840
signaling that someone was entering or leaving.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:34.740
This was a fairly large shop, but it was small enough that I could hear what was going on in the front from where I was.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.320
Which is why my heart sank, when I heard this:

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:41.120
"Put your hands up. This is a robbery."

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:47.040
I then hear a horrified scream, which I think was coming from the other customer that was in the store with me.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:51.940
"You. Don't move. Get up against the wall. I said back to the wall. Now!"

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.340
That was a different voice.

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:58.240
As far as I could tell, there were at least two men who were operating this.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.460
The entire store was suddenly silent.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:04.280
*gunshot*

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.540
That's when I heard what seemed like the loudest gunshot I've ever heard.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.240
I literally had to cover my own mouth to prevent myself from gasping or screaming,

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.460
and tried to stay as quiet as possible.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.660
"Open up the register and step away."

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.320
I heard the familiar sound of a cash register opening,

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:24.160
and it was quiet for a few moments as I could only hear people shuffling around,

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:28.920
which I assume was the guy hopping over the counter and unloading the register into a bag or something.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:34.200
After that, there was a quieter exchange between the first robber and the owner of the store.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:40.060
I couldn't hear it very clearly, but from what I could gather, the robber had asked to be taken to the vault or something like that.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:45.940
It seemed like the accomplice had stayed back with the other customer, and the lights in the entire store had been turned off.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.340
Possibly to make it look like they were closed from the outside.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.860
I thought about calling the police but I was afraid that they would hear me,

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:56.000
given how quiet it was and how well sound seemed to travel in the store.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.640
My hands were shaking as I tried texting my roommate to ask him to send help.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.420
But I was cut short when I heard two pairs of footsteps headed in my direction.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:15.680
This sent me into a panic, since I had left a couple of items on the floor.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:20.280
The door to the dressing room was a thin swinging door with diagonal upward facing slots

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:26.220
so that I could see out to the ceiling, but someone on the outside would only be able to see part of the floor if they tried to peak in.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.600
As quickly and quietly as possible,

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:31.800
I gathered up everything from the floor and moved it onto the bench.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.980
I picked my feet up onto the bench and tried to squeeze myself into the corner.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:36.780
There is a small slot under the door.

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:41.780
Not enough to fit through, but enough that you could see if someone's feet were on the ground from the other side.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:46.460
I was able to see two pairs of shoes walk right past my door

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.260
while I tried not to breath.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.780
They seemed to go into the back somewhere

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:56.100
so I decided to finish my text message and hope that my roommate would notice and contact the police for me.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:01.440
This was before I knew that some call centers allow you to send a text message to 911 directly

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.300
which is now recommended for situations that are too dangerous to talk.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:10.780
I was so nervous, as I waited for about 15 minutes while the owner and the robber were somewhere in the back.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:18.920
At no point during this experience was I ever comfortable, but there was a point where I kind of got used to the situation and my heart rated seemed to slow down a little bit.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.880
Then... out of nowhere...

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.860
*scream and gunshot*

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:25.880
This came from the back of the store.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.660
Because this happened after several minutes of complete silence,

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:31.820
I nearly had a heart attack when it happened and fell off the bench.

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:39.960
I was praying that the other robber didn't hear that, because I was convinced that the store owner was dead and I would be next if they found out about me.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:42.960
The robber then walked back past my changing room.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.160
"Do it."

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.040
"No! Please!"

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:45.540
*gunshot*

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:51.120
I sat there in shock, thinking that I might be the lone survivor of this crime with any luck.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:56.640
But whatever hope I did have was dashed, when I heard what he said next:

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.300
"Check the rest of the store."

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:05.120
I didn't dare move a muscle as I heard the two men methodically taking apart the rest of the store.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.660
I thought back to when the store owner had let me into the changing room.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.120
How he had unlocked the door to let me go in.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:17.300
I though maybe... just maybe... that they would assume that the doors were locked at all times and leave it be.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:22.800
But again, my head started burning when I saw a figure standing right outside my door through the slots,

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.700
trying to peek inside.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:28.120
He tried the doorhandle, and started loudly banging on the door!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.360
"Anybody in there? Open up!"

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.040
He then starts throwing himself against the door like a madman!

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:39.240
I can literally see the door breaking off it's hinges before my eyes.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.440
It's not going to take much more abuse, when finally...

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:47.660
*distant police sirens*

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:51.260
I hear the guy yell out "let's go" and they both run for the exit.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:54.040
The rest of the night was pretty much a blur to me.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.280
I remember the police arriving.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.280
Me being marched back through the store.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.300
Seeing police and ambulance lights.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:02.460
Seeing the bloody mess made along the wall,

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:04.360
probably from that first customer.

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:10.160
I was taken in for questioning. I probably wasn't very helpful, considering that I never saw their faces.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.560
As far as I know, neither of them were ever caught.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:19.500
It's pretty obvious to me why they decided to steal from a small costume shop just before Halloween,

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:23.060
but I still wonder why they felt the need to kill.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:27.480
Especially someone in my position who didn't even see their faces.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:32.460
I've had many nightmares about the incident, and have struggled to get the idea out of my head ever since.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:35.840
I've tried talking to therapists and friends about the situation,

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.780
and people have come up with their own theories.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:42.280
The best, and probably most haunting theory that I've heard so far,

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:48.960
Came from a witness who worked at a nearby restaurant and was getting off his shift around the time that I was in the costume store that night.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.340
After hearing about what happened in the news,

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:55.060
he theorized that the two criminals didn't do it for the money,

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.160
but rather did it for the thrill.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:02.980
I don't know if there's any truth to this, but he said he noticed two men in tuxedos walk into the shop...

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.960
...wearing animal masks.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:19.100
Thanks for sticking around for our very first Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:22.340
Special thanks to my two collaborators on this video.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:25.900
Sinister Storys was the narrator of The Scarecrow.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:32.040
She has her own Creepypasta channel where she covers some fan favorites, so send some support her way.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:37.500
The music in this episode was created by a very small YouTuber, but also one of my favorites,

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.720
by the name of OST Maker.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:43.860
If you love really high quality scores and music compositions,

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:50.100
go check out the channel and subscribe because OST Maker deserves a lot more recognition right now.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:52.380
That's going to do it for today.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:56.360
It looks like your bill comes out to $10.31.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:20:03.780
But if you like this video right now, I can waive that fee and you can have everything you just listened to, absolutely free.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:08.400
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every other week

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:10.420
and I'll see you in the next one.

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:13.480
Assuming we both survive.

